# Setup
### Docker container
To prototype the app on Expo Go, or to build the Android binaries, build (once) then run the Docker container from this directory:
```
docker build -t splatchat-frontend .
docker run -it --rm -v ./splatchat:/splatchat --network host splatchat-frontend
```

**A note on secrets**: the keystore file in `splatchat` (and the credentials, which are also in the makefile) are supposed to be a secret. I don't thing its that big of a deal for now, just don't share them. We will get new ones before publishing to whatever store.

### Installing dependencies
Only required once because they are saved to the `splatchat` directory which is mounted in the container. Within the container run:
```
npm install
```

### Manual steps to modify in the code
Unfortunately, there are some manual steps needed to make the code run.
- The first is the selection of the api endpoint, in `splatchat/api/constants.js`
By default, you will be connected to the "production" api. If it's down, please let Ismail know.
For local development that requires running and modifying the backend, switch it to the local ip address of your computer.
- The second is the path of the visualiser. Go to `splatchat/components/Visualize.js` and uncomment *1* of the relevant options. 

# Develop
### Running Expo Go
The Expo Go app allows quick development, on the phone, without having to build binaries.

Within the container, run:
```
make expogo
```
Scan the QR code with your phone (requires the Expo Go app to already be installed).
If you did not run this within the same container before, you will have to login with your expo credentials, just follow the cli prompts.
To stop, use Ctrl+C.

# Building binaries
### Building the Android Binaries
Within the container, run:
```
make build-android
```
The output apk should be named `universal.apk`. Transfer it to your phone any way you want (google drive, whatsapp) and install it.